[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one bug. Its reports hold **two problems**, sorted
below by cause (the tenant's locale and booking form, not the intake tag). The export repeats
some report ids; the table counts each report once.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

| problem | what it is | ticket | outcome |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `parser` | the shared parser reads every date month first, so day-first tenants get flipped dates | [#1](https://github.com/ojw2/kb-4471-date-reports/issues/1) | **fixed**: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`; #4471 closed 05 Oct |
| `hint` | booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field; day-first people type month first and the form reads it day first | [#2](https://github.com/ojw2/kb-4471-date-reports/issues/2) | **won't fix**: the booking-v3 form is retired |

<Callout kind="warn">
The parser fix does not cover the `hint` reports. They stop because the form is gone, not
because it was fixed. A booking-v3 report after its retirement is a new problem, not #4471.
</Callout>

## Why they were merged together

Intake tags a report from the reporter's browser locale, and decision
[0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line. Neither looks at the
tenant, so both causes landed in one ticket. The "tagged as" column above shows where the tag
and the cause disagree.

